# Mobile Performance

Performance matters because many users will be on mid-range devices and variable mobile networks.

## Lists

For large or frequently updated lists:
- prefer FlashList when installed
- provide stable keys
- avoid expensive renderItem work
- avoid nested virtualized lists
- paginate server data

Important lists:
- discovery
- conversations
- messages
- notifications

## Images

- use appropriate dimensions
- resize/compress where possible
- cache remote images
- show placeholders
- avoid loading huge originals into small avatars

## Animations

Use Reanimated for meaningful animations.

Good uses:
- screen transitions
- bottom sheets
- expanding/collapsing content
- subtle message interactions
- onboarding progress

Avoid animations that:
- delay core actions
- run continuously without purpose
- make text difficult to read

Respect reduced-motion preferences when practical.

## Rendering

Do not prematurely wrap everything in `memo`.

Optimize based on actual hot paths.

Avoid creating large derived arrays/objects during every render when a stable memoized computation is clearly beneficial.
